1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Hollywood Leading Men — Then & Now

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,135
Welcome to Hollywood Leading Men, Then and Now.

3
00:00:15,235 --> 00:00:17,157
We begin with Tom Cruise.

4
00:00:17,257 --> 00:00:24,437
A nineteen eighty nine Oscars portrait catches
him just after Top Gun made him a defining movie
star.

5
00:00:24,537 --> 00:00:31,717
A recent festival image shows the same focused
screen presence, now backed by decades of daring
action films.

6
00:00:31,817 --> 00:00:39,805
Leonardo DiCaprio moved from youthful dramatic
roles to an Oscar winning career that includes
Titanic, The Departed, and The Revenant.

7
00:00:39,905 --> 00:00:45,871
His two portraits trace a performer who keeps
choosing ambitious collaborators and very
different worlds.

8
00:00:45,971 --> 00:00:48,702
Tom Hanks brings another kind of range.

9
00:00:48,802 --> 00:00:57,599
From the playful energy of Big to the humanity of
Forrest Gump, Apollo 13, and Toy Story, he made
warmth feel cinematic.

10
00:00:57,699 --> 00:01:04,574
Look closely at these first three pairs, then see
which familiar expression has stayed with each
actor.

11
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Three more icons. Look closely at the portraits and the roles that made them familiar.

12
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,333
Now for three more leading men.

13
00:04:05,433 --> 00:04:14,660
Brad Pitt arrived with a restless edge that
carried from Thelma and Louise to Fight Club and
Once Upon a Time in Hollywood.

14
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:19,932
The years change the style, but the calm
intensity remains easy to recognize.

15
00:04:20,032 --> 00:04:26,825
Denzel Washington has brought authority and
detail to characters in Glory, Malcolm X,
Training Day, and Fences.

16
00:04:26,925 --> 00:04:31,691
His portraits frame a career built on listening
as carefully as speaking.

17
00:04:31,791 --> 00:04:41,424
George Clooney turned television charm into a
varied film career, from Ocean's Eleven to
Syriana, The Descendants, and directing work
behind the camera.

18
00:04:41,524 --> 00:04:44,262
Six careers, six different paths through
Hollywood.

19
00:04:44,362 --> 00:04:47,606
Which early and recent pairing surprised you
most?

20
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:59,700
Which early and later pairing surprised you most?
